WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.750
The head teacher showed us a chart:

2
00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.570
maths marks had doubled this year!

3
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.160
Then I read the axis.

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.560
It started at fifty.

5
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.080
Today: charts and summaries

6
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.240
that tell the truth.

7
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.850
Pick the chart for your question.

8
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:21.670
Bars compare groups, like

9
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:23.470
Monday's rain at four schools.

10
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.650
A line shows change over time,

11
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.950
like attendance week by week.

12
00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.490
And a table is fine when people

13
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:32.690
need the exact numbers.

14
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.340
Then summarise.

15
00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.570
The count says how many.

16
00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:41.470
The mean, or average, adds everything

17
00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:43.190
up and shares it out equally.

18
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.840
The median is the middle

19
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.300
value once you sort them.

20
00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:52.290
Five marks out of twenty: eleven,

21
00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:57.430
twelve, thirteen, fourteen, fifteen.

22
00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:01.810
The mean is thirteen, and

23
00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:02.810
so is the median.

24
00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:07.090
Now one mark is typed as one hundred

25
00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:09.970
and fifty instead of fifteen.

26
00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:14.650
The mean jumps to forty, out of twenty!

27
00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.760
The median stays at thirteen.

28
00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.530
The median resists a wild value;

29
00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.870
the mean gets dragged along.

30
00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:26.590
That's why you look at the data, or its

31
00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.810
chart, before you trust any summary.

32
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.380
A dot far from the others is a question

33
00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.580
to ask, not a number to average.

34
00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.910
Charts can mislead without a

35
00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:39.130
single wrong number.

36
00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.010
A bar axis that starts at fifty

37
00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:44.890
makes a small rise look huge.

38
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.360
Missing weeks hide a bad patch.

39
00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.770
And a summary with no chart

40
00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:52.070
hides the glitches.

41
00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:53.860
Quick check!

42
00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:58.770
Five marks, and one was typed as one

43
00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:01.650
hundred and fifty instead of fifteen.

44
00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.880
Which summary barely moves?

45
00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:06.720
The median.

46
00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.180
It's the middle value, so one wild

47
00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:12.300
number at the end barely moves it.

48
00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.800
The mean adds every value, so

49
00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.680
the typo drags it along.

50
00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:20.840
Fix the typo, or report the

51
00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.200
median and say why.

52
00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.450
Sensors make the same mistakes.

53
00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.650
In our school garden, a loose wire

54
00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.910
made the soil sensor read exactly

55
00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:33.850
zero, then exactly one hundred.

56
00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:37.230
On the chart, those dots jump out at once.

57
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.940
In the app, a week of soil readings.

58
00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.400
Spot the red dots, then leave them out.

59
00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:47.410
Watch the lowest reading jump from

60
00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:50.410
zero to about fifty-five, while

61
00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:51.970
the median doesn't move.

62
00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:53.970
Your turn.

63
00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.230
I want to show our school's attendance

64
00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:00.670
week by week, across the whole term.

65
00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.360
Which chart should I draw?

66
00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:07.570
A line chart: it shows change over time.

67
00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.840
Remember: bars compare groups,

68
00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.760
and lines show change.

69
00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.390
The median stands firm when

70
00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.410
the mean is dragged.

71
00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.580
And look at the chart before

72
00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:19.600
you trust a summary.

73
00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.610
Try it in class tomorrow: turn your class

74
00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.830
survey into a bar chart on the board,

75
00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.690
with the axis starting at zero.

76
00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.440
Work out the mean and the

77
00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.940
median with your pupils.

78
00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.810
Then ask: which one tells our

79
00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.930
story better, and why?
